they were like our butlers,
so you can just call them

00:11:02.723 --> 00:11:04.920
if you wanted to get something.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.140
And it was like, I didn't see
these people for two weeks,

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.200
their faces, I got them
to smile at the end.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.530
And that is leading to, I would say,

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:15.380
a digital world verse real world war.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:16.983
And we're going to have
to figure that out.

00:11:16.983 --> 00:11:19.060
Like the digital stuff is now leaking

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.400
into absolutely everything.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.530
And then they lock you down
and they keep you home,

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.440
they keep you addicted to these things.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.360
They can manipulate the algorithm

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.030
so they can make you
think all sorts of things.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:30.180
And guess what guys, when
you let it go for a month,

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.840
it seems pretty clear,
which sort of leads me

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.270
to the next thing, which
is also COVID related,

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.480
which is that COVID at this point,

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.720
and again, no matter what
I'm about to hear from Adam

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.090
and whatever has happened this month,

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.500
and I'm not saying it doesn't exist,

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.400
and actually I know somebody
that got COVID last week

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:48.400
and they were sick for three
days and then they were better.

00:11:49.248 --> 00:11:51.070
And by the way, I was at a family wedding

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:53.957
in Jersey a few days ago, and
it was to see actual people,

00:11:53.957 --> 00:11:56.190
and some people wore masks
and some people didn't.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.000
I didn't, some people did.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.600
It's okay, everyone made the decisions.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.710
I don't think it was gonna be
a super spreader event or not.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.310
As far as I know, nobody died.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:06.670
But COVID is also not just a virus anymore

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:07.900
in the traditional sense of virus.

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:10.500
But I would also say it's
a virus in the system

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.270
for whenever things get too hot.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.210
I thought a lot about this.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.410
For the last couple of years,

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.430
we've been told that
half of us are racists,

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.750
half of us are white supremacists,
all of that nonsense.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.480
And it started not to work anymore.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.500
It was becoming a meme,
it was becoming thin.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:29.140
It just wasn't working,
like it's just not true

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.790
and it wasn't working the way

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.040
that it did work for a long time.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.620
Like we were able to laugh at it.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.727
The New York Times would
call me a white supremacist

00:12:37.727 --> 00:12:40.710
and that it was like a joke
more than anything else.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:43.390
But now COVID is that new
thing that's in the system,

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:46.930
whenever it gets too hot,
whatever it is, it's like,

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.120
they could be like, "All right,
we got the delta variant,

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.850
we got the gamma variant, now
we got to lock you down again.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.660
We got to shut down your business again."

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.640
So it's never really going away.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.250
I mean, I think that's what I've come to.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.880
Now, if I'm completely off on
this, I suppose it's possible,

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:01.930
maybe I'm completely off.

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.120
I'm gonna talk to Adam in two minutes

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.160
and he's gonna tell me COVID is over,

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.140
but I suspect I am not wrong on that.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.990
And I think I've just one
or two more things for ya'.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:15.280
This is an idea that I thought a lot about

00:13:16.175 --> 00:13:19.740
before I went off the
grid and it's something

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:20.870
that I've been talking
about for about a year,

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.840
but it really seems now obvious to me.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:25.200
The old world isn't coming back

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.310
and I think we really have to accept that.

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:31.790
Like the old world, that
world of say January, 2020

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.370
right before COVID, which was pretty good,

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.560
it ain't coming back.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.740
Like the whole thing has changed.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:42.030
And look how quickly the
entire world changed.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:45.600
Does your life, does the
way you look at the world,

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.673
does it all feel way
different than it did then?

00:13:49.649 --> 00:13:50.850
Do things seem better or worse?

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.130
Is your life better or worse?

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.300
Are you personally better or worse,

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:55.040
are your relationships better or worse?

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.320
Like all of these things,
it's just not coming back,

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:02.380
and I think it's important for
us to figure out which pieces

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.630
of that old world we wanna
take with us to the new world

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.800
'cause the new world is coming,
whether we like it or not,

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.447
and I think we really
have to figure that out.

00:14:09.447 --> 00:14:12.470
And that brings me to the
last thing that I was thinking

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.630
about, and then I'll just say
one other thing personally,

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:17.770
and then bring on Adam, which
is that I think probably,

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:21.870
and I see no way around this
at this point, we kind of are

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:25.670
in a cold civil war at
this point, ideologically.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.330
Like there are a set of people
that want to burn it down

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.230
that have said that they
don't wanna negotiate.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.970
Like that this is the way the world is

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.630
and America is evil and
Western values are evil,

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.510
capitalism, all of these things.

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:37.730
And then there's these other people

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.140
who just wanna kinda live and let live

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.100
and understand that the
human experience is filled

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:43.740
with inconsistencies and a constant battle

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:44.750
to better ourselves,

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.338
but that there's nothing really perfect.

00:14:46.338 --> 00:14:49.680
Those things kind of can't
exist together, right?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.799
Like if one set of people is saying,

00:14:51.799 --> 00:14:54.520
"Let's see what we can
do and fix on the margins

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:57.000
and expand freedoms and
things are kind of messy

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.440
and we can agree to disagree,"

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:01.397
but then this other sort of
cult-like ideology is like,

00:15:01.397 --> 00:15:03.550
"No, it's our way or the highway,

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.410
or our way or we're
gonna destroy your cities

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.593
or our way or we're gonna
take all your stuff."

00:15:07.593 --> 00:15:09.880
It's like that doesn't really work.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:14.350
And the idea that you'd have
liberals versus conservatives,

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.800
people who want to change
things on the margins

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.930
versus just people who want
things to stay the same.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.540
It's like, "All right,
that tension is good

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.570
and sometimes it leans this way
and sometimes lean this way,

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.360
but now we're into something else."

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:28.960
And because I've come to that belief,

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:31.500
I really wanna focus on building things.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:32.920
That's what I've done with locals.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.380
I wanna find more of you

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.890
that are building your own businesses,

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.430
that are building new institutions

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.230
and I wanna help you however I can,

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:42.150
and that's really where
a lot of my energy is.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.600
So last thing before I bring in Carolla,

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:47.686
look, I did not have this thing on me

00:15:47.686 --> 00:15:48.970
basically for the month.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:53.260
I had to take a couple of phone
calls and my mom's dog died,

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.810
Charlie, little shout out to Charlie.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:57.805
Like I did hear a couple
things related to that,

00:15:57.805 --> 00:16:01.150
but I was not in the constant war.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:04.790
I was not in this endless
doom scrolling of Twitter

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.460
and what did these people say?

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.630
And even like, I really
didn't think about AOC

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.884
for a month, which truly is a joy.

00:16:10.884 --> 00:16:14.020
I didn't think about any of that stuff.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:17.270
I just enjoyed myself most
days at the end of the day,

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:19.240
Dave and I, we got a big green egg.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.640
We smoked an incredible amount of briskets

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.800
and tri tips and tomahawks,
and we ate great.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.530
Just everything we ate was great
and took care of ourselves.

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.480
And most nights when
my head hit the pillow,

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.980
I would say to him, "I
had a great day today.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:34.920
What a great day it was today."

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.430
And I believe that all
of us can have that.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.540
Maybe you can't have it for
a month so consistently.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.880
And I thank all of you guys

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:44.980
for letting me do this crazy thing

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.100
that I've now done for five years.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:49.040
But that's the feeling
that I want to go forward.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.210
Like, how do we balance
being engaged people,

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.700
being part of this new
digital world that is here,

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.710
whether we like it or not versus while,

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:01.580
or I should say, while at
the same time, being happy,

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.020
being real people in a
real world with people

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:06.690
and dealing with that tension.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.730
So that being said, I'm here, I'm open,

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:12.010
I am now going to hear from Adam Carolla,

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.530
who's gonna get me caught
up to speed on the world,

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.260
assuming it still exists.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.804
And let's see what I missed.

00:17:18.804 --> 00:17:20.790
I guess I'm a little, it's not nervous,

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:23.190
but I'm a little trepidatious, let's say.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.610
Carolla, are you there?

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:26.483
- I am.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.860
- Carolla, that was my
little Dave Rubin oration

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.030
to begin this thing.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.470
I'm feeling pretty good about life.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:36.770
I make a good steak
normally, but I ate well,

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:40.480
I listened to music, I worked
out, I'm feeling good, man.

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:42.730
I sense you might wreck
the whole thing here.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:46.670
- Yeah, well, I'm with
you on your philosophy.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:49.860
And I do tell people all the time,

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:54.030
now you just held your phone
up to show the audience.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.620
I couldn't hold my phone up

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:58.500
because I don't have
my phone in the studio.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:02.980
So for little tips for ins for sanity is

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:05.300
I never bring my phone in my studio

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:10.270
because there's nothing I can
do with it while I'm in here.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.121
It's just a distraction.

00:18:12.121 --> 00:18:17.121
And the rule is I'm in
the studio hours a day

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:18.580
and there's never a phone in here.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.680
So it's all gonna have to wait.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.510
And if you sort of make
some of those rules

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:26.520
for yourself, it's a better life.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:27.353
All right.

00:18:27.353 --> 00:18:29.460
- I'm telling you, man,
just not having my phone

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.540
in the morning, I try not to
bring the phone in the bedroom,

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.740
even normally when I'm not off the grid,

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:35.270
but just knowing that I'm waking up,

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:38.070
I don't know what time it is
and I'm not gonna just see

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.400
what someone said about me
on Twitter as the first thing

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.470
in the morning and it's not
gonna be the thing I end with,

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.740
but just that alone is a game changer.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:48.130
- Yeah, to answer your question, which is,

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:52.400
why isn't the media talking
about diet and exercise

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:57.400
and body mass index and
obesity and all these things,

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:02.280
which is interesting that, other than age,

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:06.560
the second most important
part of not being killed

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:11.560
by COVID is obesity and
they never bring up age

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.534
or obesity by the way.

00:19:13.534 --> 00:19:18.270
So obviously, what it is with
diet, exercise, supplements,

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.320
and the things you've been speaking about

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.350
